{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The broad `grind` call fails because it does not reliably instantiate the successor supplied by the underlying bisimilarity. Handling the two choice-transition constructors explicitly avoids expensive search: left transitions use `follow_fst`/`follow_snd`, while right transitions are matched identically and use reflexivity.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  use @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, ChoiceBisim.choice h\\n  intro s₁ s₂ hs μ\\n  constructor\\n  · intro s₁' ht\\n    cases hs with\\n    | choice h =>\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨s₂', ht, hb⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n        exact ⟨s₂', Tr.choiceL ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        exact ⟨s₁', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim (HomBisimilarity.refl _)⟩\\n    | bisim h =>\\n      obtain ⟨s₂', ht, hb⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n      exact ⟨s₂', ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\\n  · intro s₂' ht\\n    cases hs with\\n    | choice h =>\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨s₁', ht, hb⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n        exact ⟨s₁', Tr.choiceL ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        exact ⟨s₂', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim (HomBisimilarity.refl _)⟩\\n    | bisim h =>\\n      obtain ⟨s₁', ht, hb⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n      exact ⟨s₁', ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\"}"}}
